userStories.description:
**Goal** — Create the AgentStreamEvent type system and AgentStreamEventBus for live agent activity telemetry, separate from the final dispatch bus.

**Motivation** — The existing heartbeat is a parent-process liveness signal that cannot distinguish a slow model actively thinking from a wedged acpx/agent session producing no ACP updates for a long time. We need a dedicated stream event channel.

**Approach** — Define the AgentStreamEvent discriminated union with six concrete event interfaces (call_started, message_update, thinking_update, usage_update, process_update, call_ended). Implement AgentStreamEventBus with onAgentStream(listener) returning an unsubscribe function and emitAgentStream(event) with listener exception isolation. Keep payloads metadata-only by default — no raw message or thought content. Add agentStreamEvents to NaxRuntime and construct the bus in createRuntime(). Follow the existing DispatchEventBus pattern (Set-based listeners, try/catch per listener, warn-log errors). Do NOT modify DispatchEventBus — final result events and live stream events are separate channels.

**Scope** — In: AgentStreamEvent union, AgentStreamEventBus class, NaxRuntime.agentStreamEvents field, createRuntime() bus construction, barrel exports from src/runtime/index.ts. Out: changes to DispatchEventBus, ACP adapter changes, watchdog logic, TUI changes.

**Interface**
```typescript
type AgentStreamEvent =
  | AgentCallStartedEvent
  | AgentMessageUpdateEvent
  | AgentThinkingUpdateEvent
  | AgentUsageUpdateEvent
  | AgentProcessUpdateEvent
  | AgentCallEndedEvent;

interface AgentStreamEventBase {
  readonly callId: string;
  readonly runId: string;
  readonly agentName: string;
  readonly sessionName: string;
  readonly storyId?: string;
  readonly stage?: PipelineStage;
  readonly pid?: number;
  readonly timestamp: number;
}

interface AgentCallStartedEvent extends AgentStreamEventBase {
  readonly kind: "agent.call_started";
  readonly model: string;
  readonly timeoutSeconds: number;
}

interface AgentMessageUpdateEvent extends AgentStreamEventBase {
  readonly kind: "agent.message_update";
  readonly deltaBytes?: number;
}

interface AgentThinkingUpdateEvent extends AgentStreamEventBase {
  readonly kind: "agent.thinking_update";
  readonly deltaBytes?: number;
}

interface AgentUsageUpdateEvent extends AgentStreamEventBase {
  readonly kind: "agent.usage_update";
  readonly inputTokens?: number;
  readonly outputTokens?: number;
  readonly costUsd?: number;
}

interface AgentProcessUpdateEvent extends AgentStreamEventBase {
  readonly kind: "agent.process_update";
  readonly status: "spawned" | "stderr" | "cancelled" | "exited";
  readonly exitCode?: number;
}

interface AgentCallEndedEvent extends AgentStreamEventBase {
  readonly kind: "agent.call_ended";
  readonly status: "success" | "error" | "cancelled" | "timeout";
  readonly exitCode?: number;
}

export interface IAgentStreamEventBus {
  onAgentStream(listener: (event: AgentStreamEvent) => void): () => void;
  emitAgentStream(event: AgentStreamEvent): void;
}
```

**Goal** — Modify the ACP adapter layer to emit AgentStreamEvents during agent prompt execution, mapping ACP JSON-RPC session/update events to the stream event channel.

**Motivation** — Without live activity events emitted from the ACP adapter, the watchdog and TUI have no signal to distinguish actively-thinking agents from wedged sessions. The adapter layer must emit metadata-only activity events during prompt execution.

**Approach** — Add an optional stream callback to ACP client/session construction. Thread call metadata (runId, agentName, sessionName, storyId, stage, model, timeoutSeconds) through openSession() and complete(). Generate a stable UUID callId per physical prompt invocation at prompt start — not sessionName — because one session can have multiple turns. Emit agent.call_started before spawning acpx. Emit agent.process_update { status: "spawned" } after PID registration. Modify parseAcpxJsonLine() to return activity metadata for the current line while still updating parse state: agent_message_chunk → agent.message_update, agent_thought_chunk → agent.thinking_update, usage_update → agent.usage_update. Do NOT include raw message or thought content — use deltaBytes only. Emit activity events immediately while reading stdout lines, not waiting for proc.exited. Emit agent.process_update { status: "stderr" } as diagnostic metadata only. Emit agent.process_update { status: "exited" } and agent.call_ended in all terminal paths: success, non-zero exit, cancel, parse failure, thrown spawn/stream errors.

**Scope** — In: stream callback threading through adapter-lifecycle.ts, spawn-client.ts, parser.ts, adapter.ts, adapter-session-types.ts; activity metadata return from parseAcpxJsonLine(); callId generation and lifecycle event emission. Out: watchdog logic, config changes, TUI changes, failure classification.

**Interface**
```typescript
// In adapter-session-types.ts — add optional stream callback to AcpClient
interface AcpClientOptions {
  // ... existing fields
  onStreamActivity?: (event: AgentStreamEvent) => void;
}

// In parser.ts — parseAcpxJsonLine() additionally returns activity metadata
interface AcpxLineActivity {
  kind?: "message_update" | "thinking_update" | "usage_update";
  deltaBytes?: number;
  inputTokens?: number;
  outputTokens?: number;
  costUsd?: number;
}

// parseAcpxJsonLine() signature change: returns AcpxLineActivity | undefined
function parseAcpxJsonLine(line: string, state: AcpxParseState): AcpxLineActivity | undefined;
```

verifiedBy.observed:
// AC5: Emit call_started BEFORE spawning the acpx process
emit?.({
  ...baseEvent,
  kind: "agent.call_started",
  model: this.model,
  timeoutSeconds: this.timeoutSeconds,
  timestamp: now(),
});

let proc: ReturnType<typeof _spawnClientDeps.spawn>;
try {
  proc = _spawnClientDeps.spawn(cmd, {
    cwd: this.cwd,
    stdin: "pipe",
    stdout: "pipe",
    stderr: "pipe",
    env: this.env,
  });
} catch (spawnErr) {
  // Spawn itself threw before we got a PID — emit call_ended with error status
  emit?.({ ...baseEvent, kind: "agent.call_ended", status: "error", timestamp: now() });
  throw spawnErr;
}

userStories.description:
**Goal** — Implement the idle watchdog subscriber that monitors AgentStreamEvents and cancels stale prompts when no configured activity is observed within the idle timeout.

**Motivation** — The existing wall-clock timeout cannot distinguish a slow but active model from a truly wedged session. The watchdog uses prompt-level activity telemetry (not parent heartbeat) to detect and cancel stale prompts before the full wall-clock timeout.

**Approach** — Add agent.acp.idleWatchdog config schema (Zod) and runtime types (TypeScript). Implement attachAgentIdleWatchdog(agentStreamEvents, controllerRegistry, config) that subscribes to the AgentStreamEventBus. Maintain a Map<callId, WatchdogState> tracking startedAt, lastActivityAt, and counters (messageUpdates, thinkingUpdates, usageUpdates). Initialize lastActivityAt on agent.call_started. Reset lastActivityAt only for configured activityKinds (message_update, thinking_update, usage_update). Do NOT reset on agent.process_update or parent heartbeat. Implement four modes: off (no state/timers), observe (log only, no cancel), warn-then-cancel (log at threshold, wait cancelGraceSeconds, cancel if still idle), cancel (cancel immediately at threshold). Use one bounded interval timer for all active calls; delete timers/state on agent.call_ended. Track retry attempts per logical agent operation; do not exceed maxRetryAttempts. Add a prompt controller registry keyed by callId with a minimal cancellation function (wraps AcpSession.cancelActivePrompt()).

**Scope** — In: IdleWatchdogConfig schema and types, attachAgentIdleWatchdog() middleware, WatchdogState tracking, timer management, prompt controller registry, four watchdog modes. Out: ACP adapter changes, failure classification, TUI changes, logging middleware.

**Interface**
```typescript
interface IdleWatchdogConfig {
  enabled: boolean;
  mode: "off" | "observe" | "warn-then-cancel" | "cancel";
  idleTimeoutSeconds: number;
  activityKinds: Array<"message_update" | "thinking_update" | "usage_update">;
  cancelGraceSeconds: number;
  maxRetryAttempts: number;
}

interface WatchdogState {
  readonly callId: string;
  readonly agentName: string;
  readonly sessionName: string;
  readonly storyId?: string;
  readonly stage?: PipelineStage;
  readonly pid?: number;
  startedAt: number;
  lastActivityAt: number;
  messageUpdates: number;
  thinkingUpdates: number;
  usageUpdates: number;
}

function attachAgentIdleWatchdog(
  agentStreamEvents: IAgentStreamEventBus,
  controllerRegistry: Map<string, () => Promise<void>>,
  config: NaxConfig
): () => void;
```

**Goal** — Classify watchdog stale cancellations as retriable availability failures (fail-stale) and wire them through the existing retry/fallback pipeline so stale prompts can be retried or fallback agents invoked.

**Motivation** — Without proper failure classification, watchdog cancellations would be treated as generic errors, bypassing the retry infrastructure. Stale prompts should be retried with the same agent up to maxRetryAttempts, then fall back to alternate agents, just like other availability failures.

**Approach** — Add fail-stale to the AdapterFailure.outcome union in context/engine/types.ts. Classify fail-stale as category: "availability", retriable: true until maxRetryAttempts is exhausted, then retriable: false. Extend the default retry strategy (agents/retry/default-strategy.ts) to handle fail-stale alongside existing fail-rate-limit with appropriate backoff. Ensure complete() and runAsSession() return structured AdapterFailure with outcome: fail-stale — never hand failure text to operation parsers as if it were model output. Ensure SessionFailureError carries the fail-stale AdapterFailure so AgentManager can interpret it. Preserve the distinction between fail-stale (no configured stream activity within idle timeout) and fail-timeout (wall-clock timeout exceeded). Log recovery paths: same-agent retry, fallback agent selected, retries exhausted, terminal stale failure. fail-stale must NOT trigger quality escalation.

**Scope** — In: fail-stale outcome in AdapterFailure union, retry strategy extension, SessionFailureError propagation, adapter failure return paths, operation-level stale failure handling. Out: watchdog timer logic, config schema, ACP parser changes, TUI changes.

**Interface**
```typescript
// In context/engine/types.ts — AdapterFailure.outcome union gains:
| "fail-stale"

// In agents/retry/default-strategy.ts — shouldRetry extended:
// fail-stale is retriable (category: "availability") up to maxRetryAttempts

// In agents/manager.ts — AgentManager.runWithFallback:
// fail-stale failures follow same retry→fallback path as fail-rate-limit
// Retry count for fail-stale is tracked per logical agent operation
// Wall-clock timeout failures (fail-timeout) remain separate from stale-idle retry accounting
```

**Goal** — Add lightweight structured logging and real-time TUI display of agent stream events so operators can diagnose stale prompts and monitor agent activity without raw content exposure.

**Motivation** — Without observability into the stream event channel, operators cannot tell whether a prompt is actively progressing or idle. Logs and TUI should show enough metadata to diagnose a stale prompt without exposing raw message or thought content.

**Approach** — Add attachAgentStreamLogging(bus) middleware subscriber that logs call_started, call_ended, idle warnings, stale cancellations, and completion counters (messageUpdates, thinkingUpdates, usageUpdates, lastActivityAt, idleMs). Subscribe the TUI to AgentStreamEventBus in read-only mode. TUI components render: active agent, current story/stage, elapsed call time, last activity age, activity counters, and idle countdown when watchdog is enabled. TUI must NOT cancel prompts or mutate watchdog state. TUI must NOT display raw thinking content. Handle edge cases: multiple active prompts (distinct rows), absent stream events (graceful fallback), rapid event emission (no flickering or per-chunk accumulation).

**Scope** — In: attachAgentStreamLogging() middleware, TUI stream event hook, AgentPanel and App.tsx enhancements, structured stream logs with counters. Out: watchdog logic, ACP adapter changes, config schema, retry changes.

**Interface**
```typescript
function attachAgentStreamLogging(bus: IAgentStreamEventBus, runId: string): () => void;

// TUI hook (new or enhanced)
function useAgentStreamEvents(): {
  activeCalls: Map<string, {
    callId: string;
    agentName: string;
    storyId?: string;
    stage?: string;
    startedAt: number;
    lastActivityAt: number;
    messageUpdates: number;
    thinkingUpdates: number;
    usageUpdates: number;
    status: "active" | "ended";
  }>;
}
```
